</span></span></span></span></p></figcaption></figure><figure><img src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/be20bbfba341582993786f7f0/images/d4f448f8-e9d0-fa19-faee-430a2a83da98.jpeg\" width=\"298\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption><p><span><span><span><span>🎃 </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Tripping Animals</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span> gets me<br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>The Zwickel Trip</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span> Bavarian-style Lager<br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Schwein Haben</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span> Marzen<br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Pumpkin Delic </span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span>Brown Ale<br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Pig Spice Latte</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span> Stout with pumpkin, coffee &amp; milk sugar<br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Small Swell </span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span>Session West Coast IPA with Citra, Galaxy &amp; Simcoe</span></span></span></span></p></figcaption></figure></div>\n<div class=\"reader-image-row reader-brew-grid\" data-columns=\"2\"><figure><img src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/be20bbfba341582993786f7f0/images/6531e509-1f0d-7c80-a9ce-56b1710a7a52.jpeg\" width=\"298\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption><p><span><span><span><span>🫡 Some shtuff from round here<br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Aslin Sea of Space </span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span>West Coast IPA<br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Ocelot Blowin Up</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span> Lager<br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Ocelot Desire</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span> Farmhouse Ale</span></span></span></span></p></figcaption></figure><figure><img src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/be20bbfba341582993786f7f0/images/b7188a7d-aed9-b245-f91c-c9942d425867.jpeg\" width=\"298\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption><p><span><span><span><span>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Troegs Leaf Seeker</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span> West Coast IPA with </span></span></span></span><span><span><span><span>Citra, Chinook &amp; El Dorado</span></span></span></span></p>\n<p>Half Acre Daisy Cutter West Coast Pale Ale</p>\n<p>Fair Winds Atlantico Amigos Mexican Lager</p></figcaption></figure></div>\n<img src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/be20bbfba341582993786f7f0/images/79cd286b-db4f-67a7-08d8-65bfac339a43.jpeg\" width=\"520\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\">\n<p><strong><span><span><span>Claus Preisinger Puszta Blanca!</span></span></span></strong><span><span><span>: </span></span></span><span><span><span><span>A surfer turned natty winemaker, Claus Preisinger makes wine on the north shore of Lake Neusiedl in the Burgenland. You'll ntoice that \"Blanca!\" is not quite blanc, but rather a cloudy, orange hue from skin contact with the white grapes. Exciting, fun and a bit addictive with underripe apricot, lemon and a briney finish. Biodynamic, Vegan &amp; Native Yeast</span></span></span></span></p>\n<p><strong><span><span><span>Barale Fratelli Langhe Arneis</span></span></span></strong><span><span><span>: </span></span></span><span><span><span><span>\"Fratelli\" may mean brothers, but today Barale Fratelli is run by sister duo Eleanora and Gloria. The estate makes some of our favorite Barolo, but we'd be remiss not to share this delicate, mineral-driven Langhe Arneis with you. Crisp and fresh with underipe peach and apricot paired with wet stone and floral undertones. Organic, Hand Harvested.</span></span></span></span></p>\n<p><strong><span><span>Gaston Chiquet Champagne Brut \"Blanc de Blancs d'Ay\"</span></span><span><span>: </span></span></strong><span><span><span><span>In 1919, brothers Fernand and Gaston Chiquet were among the first winemakers bold enough to keep their own grapes, turn them into Champagne, and sell it themselves, a radical idea at the time that now seems completely obvious. Viola, what today we know as Grower Champagne! Sourced from seven Grand Cru parcels, we've fallen hard for this Champagne with notes of fresh pear, honeysuckle, chalky stones, and a refined mousse-like texture.</span></span></span></span></p>\n<p><strong><span>Chateau Cambon Beaujolais</span></strong><span>: </span><span><span><span><span>Perhaps some of the most soulful Beaujolais that we've ever had, this bottle comes to us from the original \"gang of four\" that started the natural wine movement. Chateau Cambon Beaujolais comes from a parcel just outside the Brouilly Cru that was planted in 1914. A serious but easy-drinking wine with pops of cranberry, cherry, and gentle tannins. Organic, unfiltered/unfined, no additives.</span></span></span></span></p>\n<p><strong><span>Bodegas Vina Ijalba Crianza</span></strong><span>: </span><span><span><span><span>Vina Ijalba calls Rioja Alta home - with cooler temperatures and higher elevation the region produces some of the most elegant Riojas. Vina Ijalba Crizana ages 12 months in oak and rests in the bottle for another 12 months before it’s released. The result is big, full-bodied and silky with notes of stewed red fruit, toasted almond, baking spices and touches of vanilla oak. Biodynamic &amp; Hand Harvested</span></span></span></span></p>\n<img src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/be20bbfba341582993786f7f0/images/21f3b82c-4eeb-6e98-0ce5-193a50c127b2.jpeg\" width=\"520\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\">\n<p>I can't think of a better way to close out summer (and toast the start of school!) than with a glass of bubbles. The collision of my personal obsession with sparkling wines and wines from Alsace led me to discover <strong>Sophie Schaal Cremant d'Alsace Extra Brut</strong>. Described by a wine critic as an eleven out of ten, I agree wholeheartedly.</p>\n<p>I have a little wine crush on Sophie Schaal. Born and raised in Burgundy,&nbsp;<span>Sophie is a Dijon-trained oenologist who met her future husband, Alsatian winemaker Julien Schaal, while working at the Paul Cluver estate in Elgin, South Africa. Julien and Sophie settled in the Franco-German borderland of Alsace where&nbsp;</span>Julien had already built his own name in the region. Sophie's label runs alongside Julien's, but with its own identity and personality: approachable AOC Alsace varietal wines made to artisan quality standards.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Sophie's wines are swoon-worthy.&nbsp;Made the same way as Champagne with second fermentation in the bottle, Sophie's Crémant d'Alsace leans entirely on Pinot Blanc.&nbsp;The wine is aged on its lees for 24 months before disgorgement, with a small dosage of 3 grams per liter added to hit the Extra Brut style.&nbsp;The result is bone dry, pristine and straight up fun. Aromas of green apples and white flowers lead the way to a palate of citrus fruit, brioche and almond. We’ve only carried Sophie Schaal Cremant d'Alsace a few weeks and I’ve definitely purchased more than a few bottles. </p>\n<p><em><span><span><span><span>This week’s writeup is brought to you by Beth</span></span></span></span></em></p>\n<img src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/be20bbfba341582993786f7f0/images/ac2639d9-7c97-6f99-4b16-27bd4f299ef2.jpeg\" width=\"612\" alt=\"breathe11x17in_2.png\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\">\n<p>Thanks for your business! See you soon, Beth, Julie &amp; Aidan and the entire Brew Crew</p>",
